<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marie of Enghien</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marie of Enghien was the heiress of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lordship-of-argos-and-nauplia">Lordship of Argos and Nauplia</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>, which she inherited from her father Guy of Enghien in the 1370s. Pressed by the Byzantine <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/despotate-of-the-morea">Despotate of the Morea</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a>, she sold the lordship to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> in 1388. The despot Theodore I seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a> first, but Venice took control, creating Venetian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nafplio">Nauplia</a>.</p></div>
